/*!
\page std_regex_dropin Drop-in for std::regex

The user-facing drop-in tour and the compatibility contract live on the
documentation site. This `/api` page is a pointer so existing deep links do
not 404.

- Tour (adopt / swap, what you gain):
  https://reche23.github.io/real-regex/drop-in/std-regex-tour.html
- Exhaustive routing contract:
  https://reche23.github.io/real-regex/drop-in/std-regex-reference.html
  (canon on GitHub: `docs/COMPATIBILITY.md`)

The object reference is \ref real::compat::basic_regex. The contract in one
sentence: **behave identically to `std::regex`, never a silent divergence.**

Under the default strict policy every accepted pattern runs `regex_search` /
`regex_match` in time linear in the input. `regex_replace` and the iterators
compose O(n) such operations — quadratic worst case, never exponential; a
nullable pattern's replace/iteration delegates to std.
*/
